THIS SESSION CARRIES 3 UNITS: threat-t4, threat-t6, threat-t5

They were put together because their files overlap, so one lookup often serves several — that is the point, and it is why you have them at once. What it is NOT is permission to merge them.

Each unit gets its OWN entry in `outcomes`, with its own verdict, its own rationale and its own findings, echoing its own id. A unit you leave out is recorded as uninvestigated, which is worse than a refutation you had to reason your way to.

Two units sharing a file do NOT share an answer: the same handler can satisfy one claim and refute another. Decide each claim on its own evidence. And a weakness you find while working one unit belongs to whichever unit's surface actually holds it — file it there, not wherever you happened to be looking.

Report every distinct weakness in EACH unit, proportional to what is actually there. These units are NOT owed equal output: one may hold eleven findings while its neighbours hold one each, and that is the correct answer when that is what the code says. Enumerate every site you can evidence — do not ration findings across units, and do not summarise several call sites into one broad finding to keep the reply short.

---

UNIT: threat-t4  SIZE: small  RISK: high/very_rare
ACTOR: remote_unauth
CLAIM: Attacker-controlled text used as a printf-style format string in parser or renderer diagnostics.
SURFACE (prose, from the threat model): md_html() input and callback (src/md4c-html.c)
ASSET: host process memory

ALREADY IN PLACE: HTML renderer writes output via callbacks rather than printf-family calls with input; not confirmed.
WHERE S2 SAW IT: baseline: BL-NAT-134; snprintf usage present in md4c-html.c, no input-as-format pattern observed in structure

CALL-GRAPH NEIGHBOURHOODS (pass one of these strings verbatim as the `community` argument to GraphSinksInCommunity or GraphCommunityOf):
  entity_lookup

FILES (1):
  src/md4c-html.c


---

UNIT: threat-t6  SIZE: medium  RISK: high/very_rare
ACTOR: remote_unauth
CLAIM: Input reaches a shell via system() or exec() in the library or its md2html driver.
SURFACE (prose, from the threat model): md_html() input and callback (src/md4c-html.c)
ASSET: host process memory

ALREADY IN PLACE: library has no process-spawning code by design; not confirmed in source.
WHERE S2 SAW IT: baseline: BL-NAT-78; no exec/system dependency in CMake or README; md2html is excluded from coverage and is not in the file inventory

CALL-GRAPH NEIGHBOURHOODS (pass one of these strings verbatim as the `community` argument to GraphSinksInCommunity or GraphCommunityOf):
  entity_lookup

FILES (2):
  src/md4c-html.c
  src/entity.c


---

UNIT: threat-t5  SIZE: medium  RISK: medium/very_rare
ACTOR: local_user
CLAIM: Race or TOCTOU between size check and use in shared parser state when the library is used from multiple threads.
SURFACE (prose, from the threat model): md_parse() input buffer (src/md4c.c)
ASSET: host process memory

ALREADY IN PLACE: parser state is per-call; no shared globals seen in structure.
WHERE S2 SAW IT: baseline: BL-NAT-362

CALL-GRAPH NEIGHBOURHOODS (pass one of these strings verbatim as the `community` argument to GraphSinksInCommunity or GraphCommunityOf):
  community-0

FILES (1):
  src/md4c.c


